      "hints": [
        "Evaluate $gg(2) = 3(6+b)+b = 18+4b = 10$ to find $b$.",
        "Use $f(14) = 2$ with $f(x) = \\frac{1}{2}x - a$ to find $a$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Form the composite expression for $gg(2)$:\n$$g(2) = 3(2) + b = 6 + b$$\n$$gg(2) = g(6 + b) = 3(6 + b) + b = 18 + 4b$$",
        "Equate $gg(2) = 10$ and solve for $b$:\n$$18 + 4b = 10 \\implies 4b = -8 \\implies b = -2$$",
        "Use the inverse property $f^{-1}(2) = 14 \\iff f(14) = 2$:\n$$f(14) = \\frac{1}{2}(14) - a = 7 - a$$",
        "Equate to $2$ and solve for $a$:\n$$7 - a = 2 \\implies a = 5$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
